70","id":3418608853,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Lw9TV","user":{"login":"fLindahl","id":18470258,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDcwMjU4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18470258?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl","html_url":"https://github.com/fLindahl","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fLindahl/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-18T15:57:02Z","updated_at":"2025-10-18T15:57:57Z","body":"We have the same problem. Using a subviewport to render a custom \"skybox\" and using that as BG, yields incorrect colors on the subviewport if we don't use linear tonemap and 1.0 exposure.\n\nAgX:\n<img width=\"1153\" height=\"641\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9af7e7f2-eaa1-420b-bb54-ded185c5958d\" />\n\nLinear:\n\n<img width=\"1149\" height=\"645\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/74a0c2db-2fec-41f4-8f15-b72adf2f5522\" />\n\nThe ocean and dark sky is rendered using a second camera to a subviewport attached to a canvas, and that canvas is used as background in Environment.\n\nIt's pretty obvious if you look at the far end/silhouette of the ship.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3418608853/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"con